-- Issue 1564 — ORDER 1 (the ACCEPTING order): `wrapimpl` is imported BEFORE `nest`.
--
-- Identical to main.mdk except that the `nest` and `wrapimpl` import lines are
-- SWAPPED. This order checks clean at exit 0 and the program prints `wrap(int)`.
--
-- This is the control, and it is what makes the pin discriminating: the two entry
-- files differ ONLY in the order of two import lines, so "the fixture has a typo"
-- cannot explain main.mdk's rejection — a typo would break this file too.
import iface.{Tag, tagOf, Wrap}
import wrapimpl
import nest.{nest}

main = println (nest 5)
